1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,873
A kite string pulls up and sideways.

2
00:00:02,873 --> 00:00:04,845
A ball flies forward and up.

3
00:00:04,845 --> 00:00:06,610
A bicycle climbs a slope.

4
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:09,310
Each one moves in a single direction.

5
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:11,755
But we usually want to know two things.

6
00:00:12,205 --> 00:00:15,939
Aarav rides ten metres up a
straight slope near his college.

7
00:00:16,289 --> 00:00:17,942
How high has he climbed?

8
00:00:17,942 --> 00:00:20,132
And how far forward has he moved?

9
00:00:20,632 --> 00:00:22,603
One arrow hides both answers.

10
00:00:22,603 --> 00:00:24,535
Today we learn to split it.

11
00:00:25,185 --> 00:00:27,674
So what does it mean to resolve a vector?

12
00:00:28,024 --> 00:00:33,091
To resolve a vector means to split it
into two vectors along chosen directions.

13
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:35,727
These two parts are called components.

14
00:00:35,727 --> 00:00:38,738
Added together, they give
back the original vector.

15
00:00:39,138 --> 00:00:41,055
Any two directions will do.

16
00:00:41,055 --> 00:00:45,698
But the easiest pair is the x axis
and the y axis, at right angles.

17
00:00:46,298 --> 00:00:47,492
Think of shadows.

18
00:00:47,492 --> 00:00:51,279
A lamp straight overhead throws
the arrow's shadow on the floor.

19
00:00:51,279 --> 00:00:52,911
That is the x component.

20
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:56,342
A lamp at the side throws
its shadow on the wall.

21
00:00:56,342 --> 00:00:57,947
That is the y component.

22
00:00:58,597 --> 00:01:01,203
Let's turn one arrow
in our motion notebook.

23
00:01:01,553 --> 00:01:03,558
Vector A is ten units long.

24
00:01:03,558 --> 00:01:05,819
At zero degrees, it lies flat.

25
00:01:05,819 --> 00:01:07,518
All of it is along x.

26
00:01:07,918 --> 00:01:09,905
Turn it up to thirty degrees.

27
00:01:09,905 --> 00:01:11,845
The x part shrinks a little.

28
00:01:11,845 --> 00:01:13,640
The y part grows to five.

29
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:17,403
At sixty degrees, the y
part is now the bigger one.

30
00:01:17,803 --> 00:01:20,847
At ninety degrees, the
arrow points straight up.

31
00:01:20,847 --> 00:01:22,261
The x part is zero.

32
00:01:22,661 --> 00:01:23,883
Watch the graph.

33
00:01:23,883 --> 00:01:26,239
The x part follows a cosine curve.

34
00:01:26,239 --> 00:01:28,496
The y part follows a sine curve.

35
00:01:28,996 --> 00:01:31,751
Now let's slow it down
past ninety degrees.

36
00:01:32,101 --> 00:01:35,450
The arrow leans left, so
the x part points left.

37
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:37,140
Its sign turns negative.

38
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:39,089
A component can be negative.

39
00:01:39,739 --> 00:01:41,649
Now, why cosine and sine?

40
00:01:41,649 --> 00:01:43,157
One step at a time.

41
00:01:43,507 --> 00:01:44,407
Step one.

42
00:01:44,316 --> 00:01:47,620
The arrow and its two parts
make a right triangle.

43
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:49,247
A is the longest side.

44
00:01:49,997 --> 00:01:50,897
Step two.

45
00:01:50,881 --> 00:01:55,883
Cos theta is the side next to the
angle, divided by the longest side.

46
00:01:55,883 --> 00:01:58,006
So A x equals A cos theta.

47
00:01:58,756 --> 00:01:59,745
Step three.

48
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:04,948
Sin theta is the side across from the
angle, divided by the longest side.

49
00:02:04,948 --> 00:02:07,065
So A y equals A sin theta.

50
00:02:07,815 --> 00:02:08,770
Step four.

51
00:02:08,770 --> 00:02:09,780
Going back.

52
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:15,105
By Pythagoras, A equals the square
root of A x squared plus A y squared.

53
00:02:15,855 --> 00:02:18,924
And tan theta equals A y divided by A x.

54
00:02:18,924 --> 00:02:20,798
That gives the direction.

55
00:02:21,548 --> 00:02:22,568
Remember this.

56
00:02:22,568 --> 00:02:25,421
Cosine goes with the
side next to the angle.

57
00:02:25,421 --> 00:02:27,978
Sine goes with the side across from it.

58
00:02:28,678 --> 00:02:31,727
Let's compare two simple
cases side by side.

59
00:02:32,078 --> 00:02:35,356
At zero degrees, cos
is one and sin is zero.

60
00:02:35,356 --> 00:02:38,552
So A x is the full ten, and A y is zero.

61
00:02:38,952 --> 00:02:42,156
At ninety degrees, cos
is zero and sin is one.

62
00:02:42,156 --> 00:02:45,183
So A x is zero, and A y is the full ten.

63
00:02:45,783 --> 00:02:46,835
Now you try.

64
00:02:46,835 --> 00:02:50,954
At forty five degrees, which
part is bigger, A x or A y?

65
00:02:50,954 --> 00:02:52,262
Pause and decide.

66
00:02:55,462 --> 00:02:56,713
They are equal!

67
00:02:56,713 --> 00:03:01,909
Cos forty five and sin forty five are
both about zero point seven oh seven.

68
00:03:01,909 --> 00:03:05,409
So each part is about
seven point oh seven units.

69
00:03:06,059 --> 00:03:07,307
Here is one more.

70
00:03:07,307 --> 00:03:10,614
Can a component ever be
longer than the vector itself?

71
00:03:10,614 --> 00:03:11,760
Pause and think.

72
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:15,860
No!

73
00:03:15,422 --> 00:03:20,194
A component is a side of the right
triangle, and the vector is the longest

74
00:03:20,194 --> 00:03:21,094
side.

75
00:03:20,757 --> 00:03:22,987
Cos and sin never go above one.

76
00:03:23,637 --> 00:03:25,464
Now, one worked example.

77
00:03:25,464 --> 00:03:27,035
Back to Aarav's slope.

78
00:03:27,385 --> 00:03:31,296
He rides ten metres up a slope
that rises at thirty degrees.

79
00:03:31,296 --> 00:03:33,472
How far forward, and how high?

80
00:03:33,972 --> 00:03:36,566
Forward is the side next to the angle.

81
00:03:36,566 --> 00:03:39,149
So forward equals ten times cos thirty.

82
00:03:39,899 --> 00:03:43,151
Cos thirty is about zero
point eight six six.

83
00:03:43,151 --> 00:03:46,509
So forward is about eight
point six six metres.

84
00:03:47,259 --> 00:03:49,916
Height is the side across from the angle.

85
00:03:49,916 --> 00:03:54,197
So height equals ten times sin
thirty, which is ten times one half.

86
00:03:54,947 --> 00:03:56,411
That is five metres.

87
00:03:56,411 --> 00:04:01,155
Check: eight point six six squared
plus five squared is about one hundred.

88
00:04:01,155 --> 00:04:02,824
Its square root is ten.

89
00:04:03,474 --> 00:04:04,940
Now, the exam trap.

90
00:04:05,290 --> 00:04:09,007
Many students think the x
component is always A cos theta.

91
00:04:09,357 --> 00:04:12,315
But it depends on where
the angle is measured.

92
00:04:12,315 --> 00:04:16,671
If theta is measured from the y
axis, then A x equals A sin theta.

93
00:04:17,321 --> 00:04:18,847
Where is this asked?

94
00:04:18,847 --> 00:04:23,620
Mostly inside bigger problems:
projectiles, forces on a slope, and adding

95
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:24,665
many vectors.

96
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,492
Exam level now.

97
00:04:26,492 --> 00:04:31,486
A vector of thirteen units has an x
component of plus twelve, and it points

98
00:04:31,486 --> 00:04:32,880
below the x axis.

99
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,211
Which is correct?

100
00:04:34,211 --> 00:04:35,491
Pause and solve.

101
00:04:40,891 --> 00:04:42,266
The answer is B.

102
00:04:42,766 --> 00:04:47,239
A y squared equals thirteen squared
minus twelve squared, which is twenty

103
00:04:47,239 --> 00:04:48,139
five.

104
00:04:47,793 --> 00:04:49,851
So the size of A y is five.

105
00:04:50,351 --> 00:04:53,872
It points below the x
axis, so A y is minus five.

106
00:04:53,872 --> 00:04:57,953
And tan of the angle is five
over twelve, below the x axis.

107
00:04:58,553 --> 00:05:00,012
Here is your recap.

108
00:05:00,012 --> 00:05:01,511
Screenshot this card.

109
00:05:04,711 --> 00:05:07,548
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

110
00:05:07,948 --> 00:05:08,848
One.

111
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:10,935
What does it mean to resolve a vector?

112
00:05:11,835 --> 00:05:12,735
Two.

113
00:05:12,305 --> 00:05:15,487
Why can a component never
be longer than the vector?

114
00:05:16,387 --> 00:05:17,287
Three.

115
00:05:17,015 --> 00:05:21,633
If the angle is measured from the
y axis, which formula gives A x?

116
00:05:22,733 --> 00:05:27,098
Next time: what if every vector could
be built from tiny arrows of length

117
00:05:27,098 --> 00:05:27,998
one?

118
00:05:27,578 --> 00:05:29,027
We meet unit vectors.
